Skip GDAL's target-Python probe when Python bindings are explicitly off.

GDAL probes for a target Python interpreter before it decides whether to build
the bindings. Cross-compiling under CMake 4.x, that probe fails policy CMP0190
("Interpreter and/or Compiler components cannot be searched when
CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR variable is not specified"). 3.13.3 guards the
probe on BUILD_PYTHON_BINDINGS_OLD_VAL, but that cache entry only exists after a
first configure, so a fresh -DBUILD_PYTHON_BINDINGS=OFF build still probes.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -221,7 +221,11 @@
 endif()
 set(ENV{MKL_ENABLE_INSTRUCTIONS} "SSE4_2")
 
-if (BUILD_PYTHON_BINDINGS OR (NOT DEFINED BUILD_PYTHON_BINDINGS_OLD_VAL))
+# Mobile cross-compile guard: upstream's condition still probes for the target
+# Python on a first configure with -DBUILD_PYTHON_BINDINGS=OFF (the _OLD_VAL
+# cache entry is not set yet), and under CMake 4.x that trips CMP0190 when
+# cross-compiling without CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR. Honour the explicit OFF.
+if (BUILD_PYTHON_BINDINGS OR (NOT DEFINED BUILD_PYTHON_BINDINGS AND NOT DEFINED BUILD_PYTHON_BINDINGS_OLD_VAL))
     if (Python_LOOKUP_VERSION)
         set(Python_FIND_STRATEGY VERSION)
         find_package(Python ${Python_LOOKUP_VERSION} EXACT COMPONENTS Interpreter Development NumPy)
